  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Sundanese bronze ensemble associated with the courts of the Priangan regents and tuned to the pentatonic degung scale, a pelog-type tuning. A bonang degung kettle-gong row leads, with saron and peking metallophones, jengglong hanging gongs (here the kempul card), goong, kendang and the four-holed suling degung; degung kawih adds a female singer to the instrumental degung klasik.",
